Test fastcore using a model with tiny values in biomass reaction\n\nThis model is consistent mathematically since there is a flux solution within the flux bounds. However, the numerical nature of the fastcore algorithm requires an epsilon-parameter indicating the minimum flux that is considered non-zero. For this reason, some models with reactions where tiny stoichiometric values appear can be seen as inconsistent by fastcore.\n\nIn this particular model, rxn_2 can take a maximum flux of 1000. At the same time rxn_1 will have to take a flux of 1e-4. This is the maximum possible flux for rxn_1 so running fastcore with an epsilon larger than 1e-4 will indicate that the model is not consistent.
